id:                     E446
trigger_tool:           meson|ctest|conan|filesystem
phase:                  testing
error_signature:        Assertion failed: !zix_create_symlink|ZIX_STATUS_BAD_PERMS|hard.?link.*BAD_PERMS|symlink.*NOT_SUPPORTED

severity:               2
category:               hmdfs, portability, testing, filesystem
match_keywords:         zix, filesystem, HMDFS, OHOS, symlink, hardlink, BAD_PERMS, NOT_SUPPORTED, meson test, canonical path
title:                  Keep filesystem tests active while exempting unsupported OHOS link-creation paths

root_cause:             Some OHOS/HMDFS-backed test directories reject hardlink or symlink creation even though ordinary file, directory, and path canonicalization operations work. Upstream filesystem tests may assert POSIX link creation success and abort before the remaining coverage runs.
affected_scope:         Small portability libraries whose upstream tests include hardlink or symlink subtests and run directly on HarmonyOS PC target filesystems.
verification_cmd:       meson test -C <build_folder> --print-errorlogs; require the filesystem test to continue past link-creation capability checks and preserve the non-link canonical-path assertions.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           capability-scoped-filesystem-test-exemption
rec_description:        Patch only the link-creation assertion. Accept documented platform statuses such as BAD_PERMS or NOT_SUPPORTED, and skip only the symlink-specific branch when creating the symlink is denied. Keep the rest of the filesystem test program enabled.
rec_command:            assert(!st || st == ZIX_STATUS_NOT_SUPPORTED || st == ZIX_STATUS_BAD_PERMS)
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               targeted-upstream-test-patch

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      move-test-root-to-link-capable-filesystem
fallback_description:   If the test is meant to validate actual link support rather than generic filesystem behavior, run it on a target directory that supports the required link operation and document that requirement.
fallback_command:       TMPDIR=<link-capable-dir> meson test -C <build_folder> --print-errorlogs
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          test-environment-selection

forbid_1_pattern:       disable.*filesystem|skip.*test_filesystem|tests.*disabled
forbid_1_reason:        The unsupported operation is only one subtest; broad skipping hides unrelated directory, path, missing-file, and cleanup behavior.
forbid_1_consequence:   The package can pass while core filesystem helpers are untested on the target.
forbid_2_pattern:       assert\\(true\\)|return 0|ignore.*all.*filesystem
forbid_2_reason:        A fake pass removes evidence that the library still handles supported filesystem operations correctly.
forbid_2_consequence:   CI no longer distinguishes platform capability limits from library regressions.
forbid_3_pattern:       chmod -R|mount.*rw|force.*symlink
forbid_3_reason:        Changing broad filesystem permissions or mounts is not a package-local adaptation and can destabilize shared runners.
forbid_3_consequence:   The fix becomes non-reproducible and may affect unrelated packages.

principles:             P010, P016
doc_file: doc/E446.md
similar_to: E050, E080
last_updated:           2026-08-25
source_event:           zix 0.8.1 shadow CI: test_filesystem symlink assertion failed before scoped OHOS patch; final run passed with 21 OK, 3 ExpectedFail, 0 Fail
authors: wxjshr <wxjshr@noreply.gitcode.com>
